  "description": "Closes the bridge from van der Veen's constant E to this corpus's c_sigma, for the whole b=1 Whitehead-chain family. Derives c_sigma = 2^{1/2-n}(n^2+m^2)^{-1/4} (n = c+d, m = 4a-c+d) from his Lemmas 1-4, correcting three slips in the published proof, and verifies it against Q_N computed directly from Lemma 1 on 20 chains. RETRACTS this probe's earlier orthant-probability closed form, which was downstream of an unchecked premise. Implies |tau_DG| = 2^{2n-2} sqrt(n^2+m^2), confirmed to 18 digits at L5a1, L6a4 and - pre-registered - L8n5, L10n100, L10n103. Makes the constant k = 2^{-1/2} derived rather than calibrated on the link side. Moduli only; the phase of E is not checked. Nothing fitted.",
